# Line endings, decided here rather than by whoever happens to clone the repo.
#
# Git for Windows installs with core.autocrlf=true, which converts CRLF to LF on
# commit and back to CRLF on checkout. That is usually invisible and harmless --
# it is the source of the "LF will be replaced by CRLF" warnings -- but it leaves
# the outcome depending on each person's local git configuration, and one file
# type here genuinely cannot tolerate CRLF.
#
# A shell script with CRLF endings does not run. On macOS, bash reads the
# carriage return as part of the last token on every line, so a here-document
# terminator becomes "PY\r", never matches, and the script dies with an
# "unexpected EOF" error pointing at the wrong line entirely. That failure has
# already cost this project one 30-minute CI round trip, and the whole point of
# recording it here is that the next person cannot reintroduce it by having a
# different git setting.
#
# The `text` attribute means "normalise to LF in the repository". `eol=` then
# pins what lands in the working copy.

# Let git decide for anything not named below.
* text=auto

# Must be LF everywhere, or they will not execute on macOS or Linux.
*.sh        text eol=lf

# Native tooling that expects Windows endings. PowerShell copes with LF, but
# these are Windows-only files and there is no reason to fight the platform.
*.ps1       text eol=crlf
*.iss       text eol=crlf

# Source, config and docs: LF in the repo, and LF on disk too, so a file edited
# on Windows and read on the Mac runner is byte-identical.
*.py        text eol=lf
*.md        text eol=lf
*.yml       text eol=lf
*.yaml      text eol=lf
*.toml      text eol=lf
*.json      text eol=lf
.gitignore  text eol=lf

# Binary: never touch these. Git's heuristics usually get it right, but a DXF is
# plain text with CRLF that some CAD tools are strict about, and a corrupted
# icon or sound is a silent failure rather than a loud one.
*.png       binary
*.ico       binary
*.icns      binary
*.wav       binary
*.zip       binary
*.dmg       binary
*.exe       binary
*.mov       binary
*.mp4       binary
*.dxf       -text
*.DXF       -text
